                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "267ca60f-dbfb-4774-945f-ec7cfbe93d39",
                        "entry_id": "42392b2a-34a8-32f4-b23b-87608ff1b9bc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "subfields"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "350dcbdd-6417-31f2-aa43-b275b4776d28",
                        "entry_id": "42392b2a-34a8-32f4-b23b-87608ff1b9bc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A smaller, more specialized area of study or occupation within a larger one"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4a26b905-1fd9-3768-867f-b329d6bf702b",
                        "entry_id": "42392b2a-34a8-32f4-b23b-87608ff1b9bc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A subring of a field, containing the multiplicative identity and closed under inversion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f421bee9-cfe1-4ff0-bde2-3c9694a0ad42",
                                "sense_id": "4a26b905-1fd9-3768-867f-b329d6bf702b",
                                "text": "Let us describe in general the subfield generated by a given element. Let K be a given field, F a subfield of K, and c an element of K. Consider those elements of K which are given by polynomial expressions of the form\n(1)#92;qquadf(c)#61;a#95;0#43;a#95;1c#43;a#95;2c²#43;...#43;a#95;ncⁿ#92;qquad#92;qquad#92;mbox#123;(each#125;a#95;i#92;mbox#123;in#125;F#92;mbox#123;).#125;\n[...]\n If f(c) and g(c) ≠ 0 are polynomial expressions like (1), their quotient f(c)/g(c) is an element of K, called a rational expression in c with coefficients in F. The set of all such quotients is a subfield; it is the field generated by F and c and is conventionally denoted by F(c), with round brackets."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb1c7eab-0071-4ccf-b240-e09e131aa988",
                                "sense_id": "4a26b905-1fd9-3768-867f-b329d6bf702b",
                                "text": "We are now in a position to describe the subfield of K generated by F and our algebraic element u. This subfield F(u) clearly contains the subdomain F[u] of all elements expressible as polynomials f(u) with coefficients in F (cf. (1)). Actually, this domain F[u] is a subfield of K. Indeed, let us find an inverse for any element f(u) ≠ 0 in F[u]. [...] This shows that F[u] is a subfield of K.\n Since, conversely, every subfield of K which contains F and u evidently contains every polynomial f(u) in F[u], we see that F[u] is the subfield of K generated by F and u."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fd95490a-2e1d-453b-831f-819e6f263a30",
                        "source_entry_id": "42392b2a-34a8-32f4-b23b-87608ff1b9bc",
                        "source_sense_description": "specialized area of study",
                        "target_lang_word": "Teilgebiet",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Teilgebiet",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e8812d7-4421-3eac-b4e8-4b030c22b62e",
                                        "entry_id": "6c7844da-207a-3071-8a08-eed6a6e37ca6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "ein einzelnes Gebiet, eine Fachrichtung innerhalb eines umfassenderen (meist wissenschaftlichen) Fachs, Bereichs oder Tätigkeitsfelds"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b6f925d-4c8a-4161-90f9-022f49aba597",
                                                "sense_id": "9e8812d7-4421-3eac-b4e8-4b030c22b62e",
                                                "text": "„Die Geophysik ist ein Teilgebiet der Geowissenschaften und gleichzeitig der Physik.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff1420a9-690d-4e5e-ab31-2887d9425b1b",
                                                "sense_id": "9e8812d7-4421-3eac-b4e8-4b030c22b62e",
                                                "text": "Wer sich auf ein einzelnes Teilgebiet seines Fachs fixiert, kann leicht zu einem Fachidioten werden."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b8fc198-034e-457d-8ae2-12383c8c68f2",
                                                "sense_id": "9e8812d7-4421-3eac-b4e8-4b030c22b62e",
                                                "text": "„Die Zahlentheorie ist ein Teilgebiet der Mathematik, das sich im weitesten Sinn mit den Eigenschaften der Zahlen beschäftigt.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
